;text-decoration-color:initial\">\r\n   81: </span><span style=\"color:rgb(211,215,207);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-moz-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">&lt;observer:observeEvent(input$goTransferArea)&gt;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-moz-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">\r\n    2: </span><span style=\"color:rgb(211,215,207);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-moz-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">shiny::runApp</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-moz-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">\r\n    1: </span><span style=\"color:rgb(211,215,207);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-moz-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">run_wallace</span>\r\n\r\n<br></div><div><br></div><div>También he tenido problemas con las variables de 30 sec, cuando enlazadas desde la nube: me lista una serie de observaciones sin datos.... pero cuando ingreso las capas, desde un archivo, funcionan sin problemas.... hasta la transferencia.</div><div><br></div><div>Alguien ya tuvo ese problema?</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>\r\n<p><strong>Subject:</strong> Issues with Model Transfer and 30-sec Variables</p><p>Hi,</p><p>I’m having trouble with the model transfer—when I try to run it, the program crashes. In the R Studio console, it shows:</p><div><div><div><div><div><span>text</span></div><div><div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div><span>Loading required package: sf  \r\nLinking to GEOS 3.11.2, GDAL 3.8.2, PROJ 9.3.1; sf_use_s2() is TRUE  \r\nWarning: Error in if: missing value where TRUE/FALSE needed  \r\n  101: as.character.POSIXt  \r\n   94: rasterTmpFile  \r\n   93: .local  \r\n   92: writeStart  \r\n   90: .local  \r\n   89: raster::crop  \r\n   83: xfer_area  \r\n   82: observe [C:\\Users\\liuid\\AppData\\Local\\R\\win-library\\4.3\\wallace\\shiny\\modules\\xfer_area.R#241]  \r\n   81: &lt;observer:observeEvent(input$goTransferArea)&gt;  \r\n    2: shiny::runApp  \r\n    1: run_wallace  </span></div><p>I’ve \r\nalso had issues with the 30-second resolution variables when linked from\r\n the cloud: it lists a series of observations with no data... But when I\r\n load the layers from a file, they work fine—until the transfer step.</p><p>Has anyone else encountered this problem?</p><p><b>Liu</b></p>\r\n\r\n<br></div>"
